 primary hyperparathyroidism, but systemic symptoms (weight loss, leukocytosis) suggest hematologic malignancy", "Inflammatory bowel disease: atypical for IBD due to lack of specific lab markers (e.g., CRP, fecal calprotectin)", "Myeloproliferative neoplasm: elevated LAP supports CML, but normal differential weakens this hypothesis", "Neoplastic syndrome (e.g., lymphoma): hypercalcemia and constitutional symptoms align, but requires additional evidence"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss", "Hypercalcemia", "Markedly elevated leukocyte count"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.12486749594375336, "posterior": 0.12486749594375336, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.44744186046511625, "posterior": 0.44744186046511625, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1560843699296917, "posterior": 0.1560843699296917, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unres